          "heading": "England centre Benhard Janse van Rensburg stretchered off after heavy collision",
          "body": "England centre Benhard Janse van Rensburg was stretchered off during Saturday’s Premiership clash between Bristol and Northampton. The incident occurred shortly before half-time following an awkward collision with Henry Pollock while attempting a tackle. The game at Ashton Gate faced an eight-minute stoppage as medical staff attended to the player. In the same fixture, Bristol’s Louis Rees-Zammit impressed with two tries, while Northampton’s Tommy Freeman struggled after being shifted into the full-back position."
