          "kicker": "Transfer interest",
          "heading": "Hector Patterson attracts Bath attention amid potential England eligibility question",
          "body": "Edinburgh scrum-half Hector Patterson has emerged as a transfer target for Bath ahead of next season as leading clubs monitor his contract situation. The 21-year-old, who represented Scotland at age-grade level and won the 2024 World Rugby U20 Trophy, is contracted only until the end of the campaign. Although he came through the Scottish system, Patterson is also eligible to represent England through a grandparent, leaving his international future open before he is capped at senior level."
